-- Give every figure an accessible name, so its /Figure in the PDF carries /Alt.
--
-- Chromium tags a <figure> ELEMENT as /Figure, and HTML has no alt attribute on
-- <figure> for it to carry. A figure whose only text is its <figcaption>
-- therefore reaches the PDF unnamed, which PDF/UA (ISO 14289-1) rejects: every
-- /Figure needs /Alt or /ActualText. Measured on a 0.12.0 deck: 21 /Figure, 8
-- with /Alt -- the <img> inside each one -- and 13 without, which is exactly
-- the 13 <figure> wrappers. WCAG has no equivalent rule and pa11y sees a
-- correctly captioned figure, so nothing in the HTML checks could report this.
--
-- The four candidates were measured in a built PDF's tag tree rather than
-- reasoned about, because three of them look equally correct on paper:
--
--   figcaption alone, no ARIA     outer /Figure has no /Alt      the bug
--   aria-label on <figure>        /Alt = the label               works
--   aria-labelledby -> caption    /Alt = the caption's text      works
--   role="none" on <figure>       wrapper is not tagged at all   DO NOT
--
-- role="none" is the trap. It removes the unnamed /Figure and so it clears the
-- failure, but a mermaid figure's <svg> is not tagged either -- measured, an
-- inline <svg> inside a div produces no structure node at all -- so the whole
-- diagram vanishes from the tag tree instead of being named. It reads as a fix
-- and is a deletion.
--
-- aria-labelledby is what this sets. The name is derived from the caption
-- already on the page, so the text exists once rather than being copied into
-- an attribute that can drift away from the caption beside it.
--
-- Runs after mermaid-figure-filter, which is what turns a mermaid code block
-- into a Figure; by this point every figure in the document is a Figure.

local n = 0

function Figure(fig)
  local long = fig.caption and fig.caption.long
  if not long or #long == 0 then
    return nil
  end
  -- An empty caption cannot name anything. Nothing this pipeline generates
  -- produces one -- pandoc's implicit_figures needs alt text to make a figure
  -- at all, and mermaid-figure-filter defaults its caption to "Diagram" -- so
  -- this is a guard against a future source of figures, not a case in hand.
  if pandoc.utils.stringify(long) == '' then
    return nil
  end

  n = n + 1
  local id = 'figure-caption-' .. n
  local first = long[1]
  if #long == 1 and (first.t == 'Plain' or first.t == 'Para') then
    -- The common shape by far: one paragraph of caption. A Span keeps the
    -- figcaption's markup inline, where a Div would introduce a block box.
    first.content = { pandoc.Span(first.content, pandoc.Attr(id, {}, {})) }
  else
    fig.caption.long = { pandoc.Div(long, pandoc.Attr(id, {}, {})) }
  end
  fig.attributes['aria-labelledby'] = id
  return fig
end
